{
	title: 'Web: buttons and linked cards flash white',
	spec: "On the web, every enabled button flashes when pressed: its whole padding box turns the page color flash (white, src/common/colors.ts) at once and the white decays exponentially (e^-5t) to nothing over about 700ms. The white is an overlay above the button's background and below its content, so a button that changes while flashing (Send to Steer, Pause to Continue: one element each) keeps flashing. A mouse flashes on pointerdown; touch, pen and keyboard (Enter, Space) on click, so a scroll that starts on a button does not flash; a mouse press flashes once, also where click is a MouseEvent (Safari). A card reached by its address (opening /<session>#<block>, its # link, or /go with a block) flashes the same way over about 2s instead of an outline, so the reader sees where they landed. Once that card has been in view and scrolls fully out of view, the address drops its #block without a new history entry and the card is no longer the target: the address names what the reader looks at, and the card's # link gives a permalink again. Browser test: a linked card flashes, and scrolling it away drops the hash. The terminal is unchanged: it has no pressed buttons and no address.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Built as: src/web/flash.ts (flash.on animates backgroundColor from --flash to the computed background with Web Animations; flash.buttons is installed by Chat). Chat.reveal flashes the card and watches it with an IntersectionObserver: dropping needs one intersecting report first (the reveal scroll), a connected card still marked .target, and a hash; then replaceState and app.aim(), as folds.set does when the linked card closes. The color comes from colors.page().flash because src/web may hold no color literals.',
		"A background-color flash with an ease-out-expo curve over 450ms read as barely anything (the user saw a faint icon tint): white fell to half within ~50ms. Now an inset box-shadow (100vmax spread, color-mix of --flash) with ten linear keyframes of e^-5t; the element's own box-shadow is kept after it. Checked in headless Chrome: the pressed Pause button is white, then becomes Continue still flashing.",
		"The page CSS comes from the running host's colors module, so a host started before page().flash existed serves no --flash and the flash was invisible; flash.ts falls back to --text (nearly white) until a host restart."
	],
	needs: ['0z'],
	foldInto: ['0z']
}
